# IT Helpdesk MCP API Test Suite
# Make sure the MCP server is running before executing these requests

#@baseUrl = https://localhost:5001/mcp
@baseUrl = https://it-helpdesk-101.azurewebsites.net/mcp
@contentType = application/json
@acceptHeader = application/json, text/event-stream

# Notes on MCP Response Format:
# - The MCP server uses Server-Sent Events (SSE) for responses
# - Responses will come in the format: event: message\ndata: {json data}
# - You'll need to parse the data part to get the actual JSON response
# - In VS Code REST Client, you'll see the raw response including the SSE formatting

# IMPORTANT: MCP Client Connection Issues
# - This MCP implementation requires POST requests for all operations
# - Some MCP clients incorrectly try to connect using GET requests, resulting in 404 errors
# - If you're developing an MCP client, ensure it uses POST for all requests
# - The server could be modified to handle GET requests by implementing a custom middleware that:
#   1. Intercepts GET requests to the /mcp endpoint
#   2. Returns a 405 Method Not Allowed with a helpful message instead of 404
#   3. Or redirects to documentation explaining the correct usage

### 1. List all MCP tools
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 1,
    "method": "tools/list",
    "params": {}
}

### 2. Initialize MCP connection
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 2,
    "method": "initialize",
    "params": {
        "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
        "capabilities": {},
        "clientInfo": {
            "name": "test-client",
            "version": "1.0.0"
        }
    }
}

### 3. Create a new helpdesk case
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 3,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
        "name": "CreateHelpdeskCase",
        "arguments": {
            "title": "New Test Case",
            "description": "This is a test case created via REST Client",
            "openedBy": "REST Client Tester",
            "priority": "Normal"
        }
    }
}

### 4. Get all helpdesk cases
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 4,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
        "name": "GetAllHelpdeskCases",
        "arguments": {}
    }
}

### 5. Search for helpdesk cases containing "test"
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 5,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
        "name": "SearchHelpdeskCases",
        "arguments": {
            "searchTerm": "test",
            "status": "Open"
        }
    }
}

### 6. Get a specific helpdesk case by ID
# Replace the caseId with an actual ID from the previous responses
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 6,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
        "name": "GetHelpdeskCase",
        "arguments": {
            "caseId": "0f66832a-35f8-4e79-a97c-53f1a366cd15"
        }
    }
}

### 7. Update a helpdesk case
# Replace the caseId with an actual ID from the previous responses
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 7,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
        "name": "UpdateHelpdeskCase",
        "arguments": {
            "caseId": "0f66832a-35f8-4e79-a97c-53f1a366cd15",
            "status": "In Progress",
            "assignedTo": "Support Team",
            "priority": "High"
        }
    }
}

### 8. Delete a helpdesk case
# Replace the caseId with an actual ID from the previous responses
# Caution: This will delete the case permanently
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 8,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
        "name": "DeleteHelpdeskCase",
        "arguments": {
            "caseId": "173a8447-5bf6-4047-8af9-1ee76000bc09"
        }
    }
}

### 9. Verify case was deleted
# Should return error or not found if the case was successfully deleted
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 9,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
        "name": "GetHelpdeskCase",
        "arguments": {
             "caseId": "173a8447-5bf6-4047-8af9-1ee76000bc09"
       }
    }
}

### 10. Search with multiple filters
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 10,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
        "name": "SearchHelpdeskCases",
        "arguments": {
            "searchTerm": "Computer",
            "status": "Open",
            "priority": "Urgent"
        }
    }
}

### 11. Create a high priority case
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 11,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
        "name": "CreateHelpdeskCase",
        "arguments": {
            "title": "Critical Server Issue",
            "description": "Production server is not responding to requests",
            "openedBy": "System Monitor",
            "priority": "Urgent"
        }
    }
}

### 12. Search for urgent cases
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 12,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
        "name": "SearchHelpdeskCases",
        "arguments": {
            "priority": "Urgent"
        }
    }
}

# Note: How to Extract and Use Case IDs
# When you get a response from creating a case or listing cases, you'll want to extract the ID for use in other requests.
# The ID will be in the response data, typically in JSON format with escaped quotes.
# For example, in the response: data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\u0022id\u0022:\u00223717b06c-d2dd-4863-ae38-7ff7bffc446e\u0022,...
# The ID is "3717b06c-d2dd-4863-ae38-7ff7bffc446e" (without quotes)
# Copy this ID and use it in requests 6, 7, 8, and 9 where caseId is needed.

### 13. Test GET request (MCP clients incorrectly using GET)
# This will now return a helpful error message or redirect to documentation
GET {{baseUrl}}
Accept: {{acceptHeader}}

### 14. Access MCP documentation
GET https://ppcjm0mv-5001.usw3.devtunnels.ms/mcp-docs.html
